{"kind":"request","text":"State refactor S3: give each retained-editor stage the evidence it requires\n\nFrom the implicit-state shortlist in a99e32d9 (audit at e50d9eeb). apps/room/page/src has not changed since the audit, at origin/main f04ff0f2. S2 landed at 3cb223b8, which releases this hold. Run it in lane C under 0d6d0fba.\n\nIn apps/room/page/src/retained-editor-data.ts, EditTask.state names a stage, but the stage does not carry its evidence. The optional lane, proposal, version and collectedSource fields and each step's attempted, answer and receiptVerified flags must agree with the state. sendStep, continueEdit and checkEditRequest each write task.state and re-derive the next step from those fields. The catch in continueEdit recomputes unknown against stopped from the step flags.\n\nIn one head:\n1. Model the task as stages that each carry their required evidence. waiting-lane holds the verified open-pr receipt. waiting-rules holds the lane and proposal. source-recorded holds the collected source fact. recorded holds the version fact. unknown holds the attempted step and its retained original request.\n2. Put every stage change in one transition function that takes the current stage and one verified step result. Keep it free of network calls.\n3. Keep network execution (reads, sendStep and the receipt follow) separate. It returns results to the transition function and writes no stage itself.\n\nKeep every current guarantee:\n- An attempted step without a verified receipt leaves the task unknown, never stopped.\n- The original signed request stays byte for byte in the loaded Page and is never resent.\n- attempted is set before the send.\n- A room or key change stops the task with \"Nothing new was sent\".\n- A refused answer keeps the earlier accepted steps.\n- checkEditRequest resolves only the last attempted step, and only under the original association.\n- The legacy and list1 workflows keep their own paths.\n- There is still no durable outbox: a reload loses the task, as it does now.\n\nKeep every user-visible message unchanged, or list each one you change. Use retained-editor.test.ts and retained-editor.scope.test.ts as witnesses. Add a characterization test only for a guarantee that no current test pins, and name it. Keep retained-editor.ts and the other callers working, and list each caller change. Regenerate apps/room/page/assets.ts with the maintained generator, and run the Page workflow at the exact head. No state-machine framework or library.\n\nRun the changed tests while you work, and npm run gate once before review, one gate at a time on this machine. Builder only; planner deploys. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","body":{"conditions":"One reviewed head on main in which each retained-editor stage carries its required evidence, one network-free transition function owns every stage change, and network execution stays separate; every listed guarantee keeps a named witness; messages and callers unchanged or listed; Page assets regenerated; changed tests plus one gate before review; checker-approved and landed.","target_head":"5a0e5660468884a04259e8560e5e169f99258b88","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}